    {
      "step_index": 1,
      "step_id_ifixit": 353934,
      "full_description": "- Unplug your refrigerator before you begin your repair.\n- If you are testing or repairing the following items, you may also need to shut off and disconnect the water supply:\n- Condenser fan motor\n- Compressor motor and thermal overload device\n- Water supply valve assembly",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/SaOfLbkeAxgmho5g.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_1_1.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 2,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354033,
      "full_description": "- Pull open the freezer door fully.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/OKxbMtWRmoXOWyaR.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_2_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/GcR3eNwYXLI2Qllc.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_2_2.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 3,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354034,
      "full_description": "- Lift and remove the upper pull-out drawer.\n- Lift and remove the main drawer bin.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/2lstsmEMiHTWgUI2.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_3_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/gkhWaS2A6wVNAVhg.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_3_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/miQiZbjUkYAZ1dFi.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_3_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 4,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354035,
      "full_description": "- Use your finger or a flat-blade screwdriver to depress the two locking tabs on the right drawer rail cover.\n- Lift the cover off of the rail and remove it.\n- Repeat this procedure for the left drawer rail cover.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/VIRitIupMYa24tnO.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_4_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/qrIEYbAKiKuqdVBB.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_4_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/n1MaTf5Mg3rZgyoH.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_4_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 5,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354036,
      "full_description": "- The drawer rail covers can be tricky to reinstall. Follow these steps to reinstall them:\n- Hold the drawer rail cover flush against the side of the drawer rail.\n- You should feel the locking tabs protruding.\n- Push the rail cover straight downward to install. It should click into place.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/MEFyDdexR14BxaWf.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_5_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/uLs4YXSkTmIIIFjp.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_5_2.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 6,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354037,
      "full_description": "- Use a Phillips screwdriver to remove the screw securing the drawer to each of the drawer slides.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/SpYpPYmrhf5JehPm.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_6_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/DWMnfT2SOUXOEaKB.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_6_2.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 7,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354038,
      "full_description": "- Lift the front of the drawer up.\n- Pull the drawer toward you to release the drawer from the drawer slides.\n- Remove the freezer drawer.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/52fl1tpPKkW2fGCO.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_7_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/TOksEKHvrCDBMprw.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_7_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/EnwpcK2kqHt15Tgf.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_7_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 8,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354049,
      "full_description": "- Use a Phillips screwdriver to remove the screws securing both left drawer slides.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/KfpJTpEXw4S5uS5H.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_8_1.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 9,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354050,
      "full_description": "- Pull the upper left drawer slide slightly towards you to release the locking tab at the rear.\n- Remove the upper left drawer slide.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/33sjwXHWewSnxDjB.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_9_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/ckSLAH5Ry2YjMlpj.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_9_2.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 10,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354051,
      "full_description": "- Pull the lower left drawer slide slightly toward you to release the locking tab at the rear.\n- Reposition the lower left drawer slide to gain access to the door switch connector.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/xkqISFknxAcNBnA2.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_10_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/rgwpBF54oShqjeSm.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_10_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/XAKPl31mJmdmU6SZ.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_10_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 11,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354052,
      "full_description": "- Squeeze the door switch connector to release it.\n- Pull the door switch connector down to disconnect it.\n- Remove the lower left drawer slide.\n- If you are removing the freezer evaporator cover, likely only the left-hand slides may need to be removed. In some cases you will need to repeat the previous three steps to remove the right slides as well.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/3yINl2YqHokG3eIO.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_11_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/EA34hqgEMxHjDLDp.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_11_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/KVfIIUChl4mSqG1W.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_11_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 12,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354055,
      "full_description": "- Use a Phillips screwdriver to remove the screws securing the ice maker to the top of the freezer compartment.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/65jVx2OUgBhX4NBP.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_12_1.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 13,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354056,
      "full_description": "- Insert a flat-blade screwdriver into the slot located on the right edge of the ice maker.\n- Pry outward with the screwdriver to release the locking tab securing the ice maker to the fridge.\n- When the tab releases, pull the right front corner of the ice maker down.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/HN6phJTbgGOAoJTL.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_13_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/6TneoZ2BSIDcyVEt.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_13_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/EuQyLxCpp2MMEDOE.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_13_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 14,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354057,
      "full_description": "- Repeat the previous operation on the left side of the ice maker to release it.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/gpLr1jom3UfnQH4O.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_14_1.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 15,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354058,
      "full_description": "- Grasp the front edge of the ice maker and pull it towards you.\n- Lower the ice maker.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/wR1MSK4oIdqHfyqi.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_15_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/FHUtX2326WhLU3ep.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_15_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/k6MjLiNlXvDdNlSM.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_15_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 16,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354059,
      "full_description": "- Squeeze the ice maker connector to release it and pull it straight out to disconnect it.\n- Remove the ice maker.",
