        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/GQICkgUxdYlQnJTJ.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_17_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/f2MLvBNSADpXGx2R.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_17_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/g6X4QtdB5daEJ6Da.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_17_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 18,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354042,
      "full_description": "- Use a Philips screwdriver to remove the screw (or screws) securing the evaporator cover.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/drRkumwCGRD13ClR.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_18_1.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 19,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354043,
      "full_description": "- Don't try to remove the evaporator cover fully, as It is still connected to the fridge with a number of wires.\n- Grasp the evaporator cover by the air vent openings and pull the top edge toward you.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/LNt2VSuO5xApujrb.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_19_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/ceUUluGInXNUDrUG.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_19_2.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 20,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354044,
      "full_description": "- Lift the evaporator cover slightly to release the tabs at the lower edge.\n- Swing the left edge of the evaporator cover toward you and lower it.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/sQCuH2S2WQXS1FWO.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_20_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/qfBo1al5ueCkbU4f.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_20_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/hhEHJTWJvSICOGg1.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_20_3.jpg"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_index": 21,
      "step_id_ifixit": 354045,
      "full_description": "- Disconnect the electrical connections in the upper left corner of the freezer.\n- Make a note of the locations of the connections for re-installation.",
      "images": [
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/pFGbEtvE44nOIGPj.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_21_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "src_url": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/FwcIZB42Rh2xVOiM.standard",
          "saved_path": "preweg_data/appliances/refrigerators/lg/lg_refrigerator/imgs/guide_167672_step_21_2.jpg"
        },
